§ `ss 17 and 18 -- who may see an individual's answers`

#ASSERT `section 17 permits the disclosure` `the person's prior written consent`
#ASSERT NOT `section 17 permits the disclosure` `the person's oral consent`
#ASSERT NOT `section 17 permits the disclosure` `industry statistics, industry exempted by the Minister`
#ASSERT `section 17 permits the disclosure` `unidentifiable, and the Minister thinks enough time has passed`
#ASSERT NOT `section 17 permits the disclosure` `unidentifiable, but the Minister does not think enough time has passed`
#ASSERT `section 17 permits the disclosure` `proceedings for an offence under this Act`
#ASSERT NOT `section 17 permits the disclosure` `proceedings for some other offence`

#ASSERT `section 18 permits disclosure to the authority` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 18 permits disclosure to the authority` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 18 permits disclosure to the authority` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 18 permits disclosure to the authority` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `the receiving authority's use is forbidden` TRUE

#ASSERT `onward disclosure is an offence` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `onward disclosure is an offence` TRUE TRUE

§ `s 23 -- census records in court`

#ASSERT NOT `the census entry is admissible` `a civil claim`
#ASSERT `the census entry is admissible` `a census prosecution of the person who made the entry`
#ASSERT NOT `the census entry is admissible` `a census prosecution of someone else`

§ `ss 18(4), 19, 20, 21 and 22 -- offences and penalties`

#ASSERT `the conduct is an offence` `refusing to answer a necessary census question`
#ASSERT NOT `the conduct is an offence` `refusing to answer a question not necessary for the census`
#ASSERT `the conduct is an offence` `knowingly giving a false answer`
#ASSERT NOT `the conduct is an offence` `giving a wrong answer by honest mistake`
#ASSERT `the conduct is an offence` `passing on information known to be unlawfully disclosed`
#ASSERT NOT `the conduct is an offence` `passing on information not known to be unlawfully disclosed`
#ASSERT `the conduct is an offence` `an officer taking a tip from a householder`
#ASSERT `the conduct is an offence` `impersonating a census officer`

#ASSERT `the maximum fine in dollars` `knowingly giving a false answer` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the maximum fine in dollars` `impersonating a census officer` EQUALS 0

#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment in months` `impersonating a census officer` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment in months` `an officer leaking an answer` EQUALS 1

#ASSERT `removing the census marks is an offence` 5
#ASSERT NOT `removing the census marks is an offence` 6

#ASSERT NOT `a census prosecution may be instituted` FALSE

